A :REGION opened and never closed runs to the end of the file; its body is
opaque payload that formatting passes through verbatim.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;
:REGION HelpText;
Free text that is never closed
  with its own indentation
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
	:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;

:REGION HelpText;
Free text that is never closed
  with its own indentation
-- diagnostics --
4:1-4:8 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':REGION' - expected ':ENDREGION'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:1-4:8 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':REGION' - expected ':ENDREGION'
